* RANGESW: open behavioural model of the range switch (TMUX1119-like SPST function), 2b scope channel.
* Written for this project; not derived from, and contains none of, TI's encrypted/PSpice model
* (which does not parse in ngspice 47, models/SOURCES.md).
* Licence: CC-BY-SA 4.0 (full text in LICENSE in this folder).
*
* Each parameter, its value and where it comes from (TMUX1119 datasheet SCDS401C, models/tmux1119/tmux1119.pdf,
* electrical tables at VDD = 3.3 V, 25 C; numbers re-read from the extracted text 2026-11-11):
*   ron   = 3.7 ohm typ, 8.8 ohm max          RON  (models/datasheet-facts.md, Sec 5.5/5.6)
*   coff  = 6 pF                              CSOFF, source off capacitance, f = 1 MHz
*   con   = 20 pF                             CS(ON)/CD(ON), on capacitance, f = 1 MHz
*   qinj  = -6 pC (RS = 0, CL = 1 nF)          QC, charge injection; NOT modelled here: see the
*                                             charge-injection case in run.py, which injects it as a current pulse
*   roff  = 1e12 ohm placeholder (leakage is 3 pA typ in the datasheet; a 3 pA leak into 1 kohm-range nodes is
*           3 nV, so it is not worth a model element)
* NOT modelled (model gap, closed by VT-4/VT-10 on the board): the dependence of ron on signal level and
* temperature, the on-capacitance split between the two pins, bulk/ESD diodes, break-before-make timing.
*
* closed: a - ron - b, with con/2 from each end to node 0 (the on capacitance split in two)
.subckt RSW_CLOSED a b params: ron=3.7 con=20p
Ron a b {ron}
Con1 a 0 {con/2}
Con2 b 0 {con/2}
.ends
* open: roff across, coff across the open channel
.subckt RSW_OPEN a b params: coff=6p roff=1e12
Roff a b {roff}
Coff a b {coff}
.ends
